REPLACE this body. The old Wix catechism pages redirect here, so this is what a
newcomer or enquirer now lands on — write it for someone who has never been to a
Coptic Orthodox liturgy and is deciding whether to come on Sunday.

Things worth answering, if the parish agrees they matter:

- When to arrive, and what happens if you are late
- How long the liturgy lasts
- Whether there is anything to dress or not dress in
- Where to sit, and whether anyone will mind where you sit
- What happens at communion, and what a visitor should do
- Whether there is coffee afterwards and whether you are expected to stay

Copy for the old lessons — "Lesson 1: Intro", "Lesson 2: Young Christ",
"Lesson 3: Saint Mina" — is still on the Wix site while it is up. Pull anything
worth keeping before the cutover; afterwards it is gone.

This file is a `.template`, so the seed script ignores it. Copy it to
`10-what-to-expect.md`, write the real content, set `published: true`, and run
`npm run content`.
